*A plane company finally alerts federal regulators to problems with its flight control systems, despite having been warned in [[2017]] and two plane crashes months prior.<ref>In [[:File:Helstrom 1x3 newspaper1.png|''The Oregon Examiner'' newspaper]], an article says, "but the company didn't alert federal regulators until 2019, months after two deadly crashes." The wording suggests the crashes were also within 2019, making March 1 the absolute earliest the company can have alerted the federal regulators. The midpoint of March 1, 2019 and the end of 2019, August 1, 2019, can therefore be used as an approximation for when the company alerted the federal regulators.</ref>{{Ref|HSNewspaper1}}
{{DubiousSectionEnd}}

====9th====
*''[[Hunting Hydra]]'' is released.<ref>In ''[[Spider-Man: Far From Home]]'', the film ''Hunting Hydra'' is shown to exist by June 27, 2024 (see [[2024]] references). This would be made after the events of March 19, 2014 (see [[2014]] references). It would take at least half a year to have been released, meaning it was released between September 19, 2014, and June 27, 2024. So, its release may be approximated to the midpoint of August 8, 2019. With most films releasing on a Friday, it may be approximated to the nearest Friday: August 9, 2019.</ref>{{Ref|SMFFH}}

