===December===
*After eighteen months in his [[Bruce Banner's House|gamma lab]], [[Bruce Banner]] manages to meld his and the [[Hulk]]'s personas into one mixed form, where he ends up with a shorter and slightly more human version of the Hulk's physicality, but his own mind.{{Ref|AE}} Hearing about the combination, the public dubs him "Smart Hulk."<ref>In ''[[A Normal Amount of Rage]]'', Bruce Banner says that his journey with the Hulk took "about 15 years, give or take." Banner became the Hulk on April 16, 2005 (see [[2000s]] references), suggesting that he became Smart Hulk in 2020. However, ''[[Marvel Studios' The Marvel Cinematic Universe: An Official Timeline]]'' places his merger in "Late 2019." To best satisfy both the book and the dialogue, it can be taken that Banner completed the merger in December 2019, almost 15 years since he became Hulk.</ref>{{Ref|SHAaL101}}
{{DubiousSection}}
*[[Alex Tilden]] and his family take a Christmas photo together.<ref>In ''[[Viaticum]]'', Alex Tilden's children are shown not to have aged substantially since they took a Christmas picture together. It can therefore be taken that the picture was taken the December prior to the events of the series, placing it in December 2019.</ref>{{Ref|HS102}}
{{DubiousSectionEnd}}
